register_gate "tests/test_graph_persistence_contract_db.py" "GRAPH PERSISTENCE CONTRACT DB GATE: PASS" "lossless graph persistence and effective-adjacency contract" "Through a real PostgreSQL governed write, persists all 20 Node and 8 Edge kinds, first-class resource metadata, column evidence, resource catalog path classes, closed content-free observability, and canonical SHA-256. It rejects unknown kinds, malformed or forged metrics, source-body sentinels, mismatched producer/schema contracts, and cross-generation patches before mutation; verifies cg3/v1 FULL writes remain behind current cg4/v2; clears both stale pre-cg4 hash claims on schema apply; and executes the real adjacency query to prove table coupling remains active while column-only evidence does not change existing review behavior." "DB readback is authoritative: any silent kind loss, nonzero unexplained exclusion, metadata loss, stale or mismatched hash, catalog drift, observability smuggling, non-atomic rejection, mixed extractor generation, adjacency behavior change, boot-contract drift, or unsafe migration fails." 64
